From: Hazel Smith <hazel@hazelesque.uk>
Subject: gate C extensions and locale data for Linux builds

On Linux the upstream ext_modules list builds the `elf` extension,
whose Linux port has bit-rotted (Solaris uint_t, DT_SUNW_FILTER,
Solaris SHA2_CTX/SHA256Update API); every import of pkg.elf outside
the pkgdepend machinery is try/except-guarded, so the mirror tools
(pkgrecv/pkgrepo) do not need it.  Conversely `_syscallat` -- plain
POSIX *at(2) calls, compiles fine on musl -- is gated to Solaris
upstream but sits unconditionally on the pkgrecv import chain
(transport -> imageconfig -> linkedimage -> altroot -> pkg.syscallat).

Swap the two: elf becomes sunos-only, _syscallat gains a Linux build.

Also gate the cffi build-script runner in build_py to the scripts
relevant on this platform, and actually wait for them -- upstream
fires them off with Popen and never wait()s, so build_ext could race
the generated .c files.

Finally, skip build_data outside sunos: the .mo/.pot machinery is
hardcoded at Solaris tool paths (/usr/gnu/bin/xgettext,
intltool-update) and the locale files it produces are only delivered
by the sunos-only data_files list anyway.

See scm-infra/kajiya/spikes/pkg-depot-investigation.md section 1 for
the per-extension verification notes.

diff --git a/src/setup.py b/src/setup.py
--- a/src/setup.py
+++ b/src/setup.py
@@ -1126,15 +1126,26 @@
                 for path in os.listdir(cffi_dir):
                         if not path.startswith("build_"):
                                 continue
+                        # On Linux only _syscallat is built; the other
+                        # cffi extensions (_arch, _pspawn, _sysattr,
+                        # _sha512_t) are Solaris-only and their build
+                        # scripts fail to compile here.
+                        if osname != 'sunos' and path != "build_syscallat.py":
+                                continue
                         path = os.path.join(cffi_dir, path)
                         # make scripts executable
                         os.chmod(path,
                             os.stat(path).st_mode
                             | stat.S_IXUSR | stat.S_IXGRP | stat.S_IXOTH)
 
-                        # run the scripts
+                        # run the scripts; wait so the generated .c
+                        # files exist before build_ext compiles them
+                        # (upstream fired these off without waiting).
                         p = subprocess.Popen(
                             [sys.executable, path])
+                        if p.wait() != 0:
+                                raise DistutilsError(
+                                    "cffi build script failed: " + path)
 
                 return ret
 
@@ -1234,6 +1245,12 @@
                 pass
 
         def run(self):
+                # The locale data built here is only delivered by the
+                # sunos data_files list, and the i18n tools are
+                # hardcoded at Solaris paths (/usr/gnu/bin/xgettext);
+                # skip the whole step elsewhere.
+                if osname != 'sunos':
+                        return
                 # Anything that gets created here should get deleted in
                 # clean_func.run() below.
                 i18n_check()
@@ -1489,9 +1506,14 @@
                 [('po/pkg.pot', 'pkg.pot')])
         ]
 
-if osname == 'sunos' or osname == "linux":
+if osname == 'sunos':
         # Unix platforms which the elf extension has been ported to
-        # are specified here, so they are built automatically
+        # are specified here, so they are built automatically.
+        # Linux is excluded: the Linux port of the elf extension has
+        # bit-rotted (Solaris uint_t, DT_SUNW_FILTER, Solaris SHA2
+        # API) and every importer of pkg.elf except the pkgdepend
+        # machinery guards the import with try/except, so it is not
+        # needed for the mirror tools (pkgrecv/pkgrepo).
         elf_libraries = ['elf']
         ext_modules += [
                 Extension(
@@ -1562,6 +1584,25 @@
                     ]
         else:
             elf_libraries += [ 'ssl' ]
+
+if osname == "linux":
+        # _syscallat is plain POSIX *at(2) calls and sits on the
+        # pkgrecv import chain (transport -> imageconfig ->
+        # linkedimage -> altroot imports pkg.syscallat
+        # unconditionally); upstream merely forgot to list it for
+        # Linux.  The remaining cffi extensions (_arch, _pspawn,
+        # _sysattr, _sha512_t) are Solaris-only and stay gated.
+        ext_modules += [
+                Extension(
+                        '_syscallat',
+                        syscallat_srcs,
+                        include_dirs = include_dirs,
+                        extra_compile_args = compile_args,
+                        extra_link_args = link_args,
+                        define_macros = [('_FILE_OFFSET_BITS', '64')],
+                        build_64 = True
+                        ),
+                ]
 
 setup(cmdclass = cmdclasses,
     name = 'pkg',
